{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type","id":880298,"title":"My attempt at making a hybrid shifter type","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-02T11:11:32-07:00","id":880298,"title":"My attempt at making a hybrid shifter type","content":"Around the time just after started getting all the breed books, and was interested also in Mage the Ascension, i started wondering WHY canonically you could NOT make 'mixed breed' shifters, and all the book says is 'gaia won't allow it'. BUT with Mages use of spirit, mind, body and matter magic, Why couldn't THEY force it? So for a fits and grins game (lots of beer drinking) i made up the Denier, my attempt at doing a 'hybrid shifter'...<br /> <br /> The Denier (pronounced De Nay Yar).<br /> <b>History</b>: Back in the early to mid 1950s, the Technocracy held a meeting of all their various mage traditions to discuss problems and achieve solutions, to hold their course for the next 50 years), during that meeting the Progenitors brought up the fact that a number of facilities in recent years were lost to Garou and other Fera attacks. After a long debate, it was decreed that the 'shifter' problem was to be their go to issue to resolve in that 50 year time frame.<br /> During studies of captured shifters, it was discovered that those of the &quot;Metis&quot; branch were not only deformed in someway, but the most significant was that they were sterile. So someone got the hair-brained idea to see what would happen if you combined 2 different shifter folk. Surely they would be even MORE hamstrung..<br /> <br /> Over the next 20 years, they spent time capturing more and more Fera, taking care to ensure they had an even mix of all the types they knew of, then started combining their magical powers over Spirit, Mind, Body and Matter to try and &quot;crack the code&quot;. It wasn't till the mid 80s, when DNA manipulation in the world at large became more prevalent, till they made a break through. <br /> By the end of that 50 year time frame, the operation (known only as Project Eldorado), had almost 300 such cross-breed shifter offspring amongst their test subjects. BUT the overarching leaders felt that since these hybrids were not more deformed, let alone substantially worse off (well to what the Mages could see), that the project was a failure. So it was decreed that the project would get terminated... with extreme prejudice. <br /> <br /> During the next 3 months, many of the scientists (mostly mundane humans with little to know morals, but a love of science) along with well over half the cross-breeds created were killed off, and all 5 of the facilities destroyed. But just over 40 did manage to escape captivity and the termination process. After 1 year, depression kicked in and almost a dozen of that remaining stock had committed suicide, rather than live the life that they were 'dealt'. <br /> Now the remaining 30 or so, try to live on in a world that seems to shun the heck out of them, even to the point of hunting them down...<br /> <br /> Because of how they were created, Most other Fera do not see the Denier as proper shifters, and do not associate with them, though some at least take pity on their plight. Catiff and loner shifters though, do and have associated with them. <br /> <br /> <b>Character creation rules</b>:<br /> Of the 30 or so types that were remaining at the end of the Project, one was a Mokole Gurahl (father/mother) hybrid. Two were Corax Garou, 4 were Garou Gurahl, 5 Bastet Gurahl, and 6 Mokole Bastet. The remaining 4 were of 'unknown parentage (allowing PCs who select them to pick their parents, though note No Corax Gurahl, Ratkin anything else, Nuwisha - something else or Ananasi anything else were successfully created.<br /> <br /> Build attributes and abilities as standard for any shifter type. 7/5/3 &amp; 13/9/5<br /> For the changing forms stat modifiers (Crinos etc) use the Father's breed type to get Strength, Stamina and Manipulation modifiers, and the Mother's breed type for Dexterity mods and any Appearance mods.<br /> <br /> For the Auspice roll 1d10 to get which it is; 1-2 Ragbash, 3-4 Galliard, 5-6 Ahroun, 7-8 Phillodox, 9-10 Theurge.<br /> <br /> <u>Rage:</u> By auspice<br /> <br /> <u>Willpower:</u> As per Father's breed (If Garou, this is 4 which is the average of all the 13 tribes), costs 20% more than normal to increase via XP regardless of if in a Sept or pack or not. Can only purchase up to 3 additional willpower with Freebie points.<br /> <br /> <u>Gnosis:</u> 4 starting up (1 more than Metis get, which is a lingering effects of all the spirit magics used on them, but it is offset with a higher cost to improve). If using Freebie points to raise, cost is at normal, but has a 7 cap. If purchasing/improving with experience in game, cost is Double until they have a MINIMUM of 6 months being cleansed in the silver lake known as Erebus.<br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds</u>: 1 starting out only unless uses freebies to select more. This is placed in Past-life tied to their parents. <br /> <br /> <u>Renown</u>: 4 dots starting out, but gaining renown is hard as heck. If not accepted or a member of a pack or Sept, it is earned at only 1/3rd the normal rate. If they have somehow been accepted by a pack, its at half the rate. And on the rare occasion they may get accepted into a Sept, the cost is still only 3/4 the rate. When figuring out renown, go by Mother's breed for the types they have.<br /> <br /> <u>Gifts:</u> 3 starting out. As with Renown, cost to learn any new ones is higher unless in Sept or pack, this is cause spirits are harder to appease. Pick one from their Auspice, Father's breed and Metis. Cannot use Freebie points to acquire more. When using XP to buy more, cost is 2 times normal if not in either a pack or Sept. 50% more if only in a pack. If in a Sept, cost is regular though. These were picked up from either their parents, or from lone Fera who took pity on them.<br /> <br /> <u>Additional Hindrances and advantages:</u> <br /> For all the above few benefits (1 more renown and Gnosis than normal) and penalties (higher costs to gain any new stuff), they suffer a number of additional issues.<br /> 1) Use Mother's breed type to see what additional NORMAL advantages the shifter would have, this does NOT apply if either parent was a Mokole or Gurahl (see below)<br /> 2) Free merit of Silver (or gold if Mokole/Corax) Tolerance. This is a lingering effect of their spirits being messed with by magic<br /> 3) Can not naturally heal wounds of Lethal or Aggravated level, only can heal with gifts or fetishes. Bashing damage healed at 3/4 the speed.<br /> 4) Use Father's breed form for any Normal additional penalties they might have<br /> 5) Like Metis they have a disfigurement, but they also gain a Derangement, which normally has something to do with Mages or magic.<br /> 6) If either parent was Mokole, they only get the 3 changing forms like Mokole do, and as such gain archid traits, but one LESS than their Gnosis would normally let them purchase. Also their 'gator' side takes a more prominent position in any appearance they have.<br /> 7) If either parent was Gurahl, they go by the bear-folk's way of spending rage.<br /> 8) Besides the cost of Gnosis going down, if they ever spend 6 months (or longer) in Erebus getting cleansed, they regain their natural healing for Aggravated and Lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T15:39:36-07:00","id":880534,"title":"","content":"you put a lot of thought into something quite silly.<br /> <br /> If you want to make your own shifter, and blame mages, it'd be a from-scratch job of combining man,soul,spirit and animal. You'd need spheres at 6+ most like. Hey; If pentex can make mockery breeds, Mages should be able to make what they want (though getting it right or not is a difficult question).<br /> <br /> You don't need to do something quite so silly as having a hyena-crow. There's billions of species that you can use. Beetle,Mantis,Falcon,Crab,possum,wolverine, whatever. You could even (not likely intentionally) revive one of the lost breeds, though they might be different than before.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts<br /> -They won't be tied to luna or helios, so no gold or silver weakness.<br /> -The ability to step sideways is a possibility, but it's likely they won't be able to do it without spirit ties.<br /> -They likely won't start with good spirit relations. At best, no gifts beyond level 3 for the next few decades. At worst, spirits go out of their way to attack the offending changer. Banes might be generous though... but you're most likely to have them get no gifts unless you do a supreme job of it. <br /> - Chances are, the forms might be incomplete. You might be missing the animal form. You might be missing the human form. There might not be a warform, or they have an equivelent to hispo but not a glabro.<br /> - Deformity. an appearance rating of two might be the best they can get, or they might all be mad. Worst is most of them could be sterile.<br /> -They may or may not possess rage and gnosis (or a blood pool), but if you're doing this to a mage it'll be different. I think the arete would take precedence. The ability to heal quickly and soak aggravated is also a thing of chance.<br /> - you might be treading on ground already covered. maybe you make lizardmen despite the existence of mokole- I mean, Mokole aren't known about, but everyone want's a lizard men. Pentex did this with war-wolves, but they're somewhat incomplete.<br /> <br /> Read book of the wyrm. it's got some nice inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 05-02-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T15:48:15-07:00","id":880538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880534#post880534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you put a lot of thought into something quite silly.<br /> <br /> If you want to make your own shifter, and blame mages, it'd be a from-scratch job of combining man,soul,spirit and animal. You'd need spheres at 6+ most like. Hey; If pentex can make mockery breeds, Mages should be able to make what they want (though getting it right or not is a difficult question).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mockery Breeds are nowhere near as... coherent as actual Changers. Also, Werewolf antagonists doing this in a Werewolf game tends to lend them more of a primal air that Mages in a Mage game lack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't need to do something quite so silly as having a hyena-crow. There's billions of species that you can use.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts<br /> -They won't be tied to luna or helios, so no gold or silver weakness. </div> </div> </div>But if you're going with mockery breeds, they'll often be vulnerable to much easier to find, mundane things, such as pesticides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -The ability to step sideways is a possibility, but it's likely they won't be able to do it without spirit ties.<br /> -They likely won't start with good spirit relations. At best, no gifts beyond level 3 for the next few decades. At worst, spirits go out of their way to attack the offending changer. Banes might be generous though... </div> </div> </div>More like no Gifts at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:41:32-07:00","id":880606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880534#post880534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you put a lot of thought into something quite silly.<br /> <br /> If you want to make your own shifter, and blame mages, it'd be a from-scratch job of combining man,soul,spirit and animal. You'd need spheres at 6+ most like. Hey; If pentex can make mockery breeds, Mages should be able to make what they want (though getting it right or not is a difficult question).<br /> <br /> You don't need to do something quite so silly as having a hyena-crow. There's billions of species that you can use. Beetle,Mantis,Falcon,Crab,possum,wolverine, whatever. You could even (not likely intentionally) revive one of the lost breeds, though they might be different than before.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read the history, you would see why the mages went that route rather than 'doing designer shifters' like Pentex has done..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880534#post880534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts<br /> -They won't be tied to luna or helios, so no gold or silver weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was covered in the write up for benefits they get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880534#post880534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The ability to step sideways is a possibility, but it's likely they won't be able to do it without spirit ties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.. never thought of that angle. If anything i would see them still being able to do it, but at a penalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880534#post880534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-They likely won't start with good spirit relations. At best, no gifts beyond level 3 for the next few decades. At worst, spirits go out of their way to attack the offending changer. Banes might be generous though... but you're most likely to have them get no gifts unless you do a supreme job of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the write up again. It mentions that they have big difficulties in learning new skills (Costs doubled unless they somehow get accepted into a pact or sept).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880534#post880534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Chances are, the forms might be incomplete. You might be missing the animal form. You might be missing the human form. There might not be a warform, or they have an equivelent to hispo but not a glabro.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of that, but felt that they should still get them for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880534#post880534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Deformity. an appearance rating of two might be the best they can get, or they might all be mad. Worst is most of them could be sterile.</div> </div> </div> </div>You obviously didn't read it all did you. Again that was already covered. 1) they gain a disfigurement, 2) they gain a derangement and 3) they are sterile like metis are..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880534#post880534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-They may or may not possess rage and gnosis (or a blood pool), but if you're doing this to a mage it'll be different. I think the arete would take precedence. The ability to heal quickly and soak aggravated is also a thing of chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are covered on the rage/gnosis angle, but the latter is a lot harder to gain new ones of via XP.. As for healing, yes it is also covered. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:42:06-07:00","id":880607,"title":"","content":"PS mods.. i just realized this was in the general forum, vice werewolf specific sub-forum. Can you move it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:30:50-07:00","id":880642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880606#post880606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1 If you read the history, you would see why the mages went that route rather than 'doing designer shifters' like Pentex has done..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2 That was covered in the write up for benefits they get.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3 Hmm.. never thought of that angle. If anything i would see them still being able to do it, but at a penalty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 4 See the write up again. It mentions that they have big difficulties in learning new skills (Costs doubled unless they somehow get accepted into a pact or sept).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 5 I thought of that, but felt that they should still get them for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 6 You obviously didn't read it all did you. Again that was already covered. 1) they gain a disfigurement, 2) they gain a derangement and 3) they are sterile like metis are..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They are covered on the rage/gnosis angle, but the latter is a lot harder to gain new ones of via XP.. As for healing, yes it is also covered.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1- your history explains... well... it's... Given how smart the technocracy are none of this would happen.<br /> <br /> Scientist 1- let's wipe out the shifters, they're a thorn in our progrom<br /> Scientist 2 (stooge)- Sure. My cunning progenitor plan is to make more shifters. They will be hybrids.<br /> Scientist 1- what effect will that have on the enemy?<br /> Scientist 2- Well, at best, they'll make them a little upset about us making useless and ineffectual abominations. Maybe if the population at large finds out then everyone will put their faith in science and it's ability to create abominations.<br /> Scientist 1- I'm calling NWO, you are to submit to reconditioning.<br /> Scientist 3 (progenitor)- I'll make a biological weapon that will specifically target this brand of reality deviants<br /> Scientist 1- Good man<br /> Scientist 4 (progenitor) I'll try to harness their shifting powers for our own ends, creating troops of equal capability. .<br /> Scientist 1- Good man<br /> Scientist 5 (ITX) I'll make super awesome anti-shifter weapons and devices.<br /> Scientist 1-Good man. Why did we hire that stooge when we've got people who get things done?<br /> <br /> 2- Yeah, nah, that's not how it works.<br /> <br /> 3- they can or they can't or they do it a different way. It's not the same thing but more difficult.<br /> <br /> 4- No. The spirits refuse to teach them. They're probably not even aware of spirits. In the unlikely event that they do learn gifts, the current model, as suggested by the yeren, is that they learn gifts at the normal cost (from banes).<br /> <br /> Also. Join a sept or a pack or a tribe or a... Yeah man these aren't even going to be allowed near wave sentai or the ahadi.<br /> <br /> 5- Just so you know, if you cross shifter with shifter, they'll be born into the form of their mother, and if the mother was the changer in question, and the kid bred true, it'd be what the mother is. Not breeding true ever or miscarages are far more likely than making a hybrid<br /> <br /> 6/7 i read it all. I'm just not seeing the point of these characters. Totaly have no merit to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Additional notes.<br /> -These fellas won't develop a renown system.<br /> -They won't survive meeting another changer.<br /> -They're terrible reality deviants with no greater purpose and the Technocracy should kill easily them.<br /> -The progenitor who actually attempts this will get reconditioned, as will the idiot who funded him. Who'd fund him?<br /> - A progenitor wouldn't even want to do this, even if he'd just had bad a bad day with the unseelie and the entire malkavian clan.<br /> <br /> -The technocracy, Like DNA, Is almost entirely unknowing of other changing breeds. There's Lupines and then there's rumors. They're probably more familiar with pentex creations than bastet.<br /> -While a few progenitors would be happy to experiment with making chimera, changing chimera... It's a mess, and under no circumstances would they be able to do it in a way that get's the strength of either creature. I'm pretty sure they'd die in their first change when their misplaced organs get tangled and torn up.<br /> - The technocracy really have a terrible grasp of the spirit sphere.<br /> <br /> -There is literally no reason for these guys to exist. This is why I offered you a viable alternative in their own creation.<br /> - The only possibility for a 'hybrid changer' is, well, stuff like tiger/lion crossbreeds. Gaia might even be cool with that.<br /> <br /> -The maths in you're using for xp costs (IE this is 20% more) doesn't work.<br /> -Erebus. Depending on your book, either erebus is only for garou, or you've got two entirely different spiritual hells waiting for you. then again you're not going to be a spiritual creature. It's a mess man. A mess. <br /> <br /> By all means make new shifters but do the technocracy some credit and make stuff seem logical or feasible or at least on the right page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 05-02-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T19:52:50-07:00","id":880679,"title":"","content":"Doesn't need to be the Technocracy that conjured up these aberrant creatures. Why you would impose restrictions on what kind of crossbreed abomination you can play as is beyond me.<br /> <br /> I mean who wouldn't want to play a spider-bear-lizard-man? Or simply skip the man part altogether, who's to say these rogue mages didn't decide to just cram a bunch of different species into a blender and see what sticks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T23:08:08-07:00","id":880762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880642#post880642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 4- No. The spirits refuse to teach them. They're probably not even aware of spirits. In the unlikely event that they do learn gifts, the current model, as suggested by the yeren, is that they learn gifts at the normal cost (from banes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ronin are also out of normal society and THEY can learn gifts.. Also not all gifts Need the spirits..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880642#post880642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also. Join a sept or a pack or a tribe or a... Yeah man these aren't even going to be allowed near wave sentai or the ahadi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't ronin get let into septs??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880642#post880642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additional notes.<br /> -These fellas won't develop a renown system.<br /> -They won't survive meeting another changer.</div> </div> </div> </div>See above on ronin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880642#post880642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> -The maths in you're using for xp costs (IE this is 20% more) doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880642#post880642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Erebus. Depending on your book, either erebus is only for garou, or you've got two entirely different spiritual hells waiting for you. then again you're not going to be a spiritual creature. It's a mess man. A mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my reading on them, Erebus seems NOT just for Garou, but all Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kristviljan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880679#post880679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why you would impose restrictions on what kind of crossbreed abomination you can play as is beyond me.<br /> <br /> I mean who wouldn't want to play a spider-bear-lizard-man? Or simply skip the man part altogether, who's to say these rogue mages didn't decide to just cram a bunch of different species into a blender and see what sticks?</div> </div> </div> </div>When i was writing them up, i felt some of the shifter types couldn't combine. Such as Corax-Gurahl, or the were-spiders with anything..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:15:44-07:00","id":880841,"title":"","content":"You think ronin are comparable? You think Corax-Gurahl don't work but mokole-gurahl do? Ah man you're in that stage where you're all super excited for stuff and want to think of the craziest stuff, but you've not yet learned or matured enough to do something proper. It's ok, Sometimes even White wolf do this stuff in publications. I too went through the phase where I wanted to play an awakened gargoyle-lupine with fae blood. It's part of the reason why I'm giving you feedback and not dismissing you as just another malk. <br /> You'll grow out of it. Trust me. This kind of line of thought is antithetical to the way the world of darkness works. <br /> <br /> Ok. Ronin are still garou, they're just not part of a tribe. That's it. They're still full garou, they're still gaia's warriors and luna's still blessed them with auspice. <br /> you're talking about things more trash than the mockery breeds. <br /> <br /> Also It's literally the worst plan to deal with the changing breed problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:51:08-07:00","id":880901,"title":"","content":"Only a sept that's pretty remote or desperate would allow a ronin to step one foot on the bawn, they are the lone wolves and they bring nothing but trouble and possible wyrm taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:49:29-07:00","id":881138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880841#post880841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think ronin are comparable? You think Corax-Gurahl don't work but mokole-gurahl do? Ah man you're in that stage where you're all super excited for stuff and want to think of the craziest stuff, but you've not yet learned or matured enough to do something proper. It's ok, Sometimes even White wolf do this stuff in publications. I too went through the phase where I wanted to play an awakened gargoyle-lupine with fae blood. It's part of the reason why I'm giving you feedback and not dismissing you as just another malk.<br /> You'll grow out of it. Trust me. This kind of line of thought is antithetical to the way the world of darkness works.<br /> <br /> Ok. Ronin are still garou, they're just not part of a tribe. That's it. They're still full garou, they're still gaia's warriors and luna's still blessed them with auspice.<br /> you're talking about things more trash than the mockery breeds.<br /> <br /> Also It's literally the worst plan to deal with the changing breed problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off innocent, this was all wrote up almost 20 years ago when i was deep into my were/vamp gaming back on NOB norfolk in the mid 90s. Its not something new..<br /> 2ndly as the writer of it, I decided that certain shifter type's couldn't be combined, just cause it made sense to ME at the time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=880901#post880901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only a sept that's pretty remote or desperate would allow a ronin to step one foot on the bawn, they are the lone wolves and they bring nothing but trouble and possible wyrm taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>What of a caern of unity, or peace? Wouldn't they be more willing to accept Ronin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:31:32-07:00","id":881380,"title":"","content":"I like how your trying to loop hole these things but really it's just cementing the impossible snowflake status. <br /> <br /> In the end though it's your game to run and if you wanna use them who are we to judge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 05-03-2016, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:15:58-07:00","id":881510,"title":"","content":"Well, so far as a ST, i have had only 2 players even express an interest in playing one. Of those 2 one went for Gurahl/Garou, and the other a bastet/gurahl. Neither played them for long as the 2nd combat our group had where we were using as a trial run to see if we trusted them enough, they died.. BADLY. <br /> As a player, i have one i made an effective NPC after taking him into my games as a ST.. A Gurahl Mokole cross.. His derangement is he automatically frenzies on the site of mages.. Roll 1d. Odds its a fox frenzy, evens its a fight frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T03:21:01-07:00","id":881625,"title":"","content":"So the guy freaks out at Harry Potter conventions? Because clearly you can spot a mage simply by how they dress....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:29:25-07:00","id":881678,"title":"","content":"How does he even know who a Mage is and how do you qualify &quot;On Sight&quot; ?<br /> I mean, in theory a homid Theurge with flashy gifts and/or talens could look the same outwardly as a Mage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T11:33:13-07:00","id":882034,"title":"","content":"He 'knew them on site' via one of the gifts (can't remember its name right now' that shows auras around people...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:12:50-07:00","id":882219,"title":"","content":"There's no werewolf equivalent to a vampire's aura perception. Also, Mages... Well. They're a disparate bunch. They don't have one set of traditions. I'm pretty sure some of them think magic is false and they're part of some sort of technocracy. (Ok, Yeah, I took that one too far) So before your player goes full marauder on the nearby coven; Think for a moment, Why is he really killing Neph and andy? <br /> <br /> Also, Yeah, My Get of Fenrir ragabash used to declare herself a wizard when dealing with non-changing supes. Still does. We don't want vampires knowing we're active in the cities, Do we? <br /> <br /> Yeah but man this is way too much effort for a drunk game. If I'm really really hammered I don't want to be trying to figure out the mathematics of a Ratea. It's dumb. Not in a good way. I'd be spending more time making the character than playing him. If I wanted dumb fun I'd bring a ratkin, Troll,etherite and a formor to elysium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T02:34:27-07:00","id":882702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880298-my-attempt-at-making-a-hybrid-shifter-type?p=882034#post882034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He 'knew them on site' via one of the gifts (can't remember its name right now' that shows auras around people...</div> </div> </div> </div>So he has it constantly on, or are you just fine with him having a flaw that will practically never come into play considering the rarity of Mages, and the fact that he can just chose to not use the power? Also what's a Mage? True Mage? Sorceror? Thaumaturgist? Psychic? Ju-Fu practitioner?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:10:03-07:00","id":882963,"title":"","content":"True mage and sorcerers was what the initial ST had when i first started running him, with it coming in when the gift was active. IF i can find the write up for it, i will post the gift (assuming i still have the doc with it listed). When i shifted to using him as an NPC when I was ST, i just converted it to practically always on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}